ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Kojève and Law: A Critical Examination","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316262447/","description":"Alexandre Kojève (1902–1968) was one of the major philosophers of the twentieth century. His famous lectures on Hegel and his provocative end-of-history thesis left an indelible mark on contemporary thought. By the end of the Second World War, he abandoned academic philosophy to embark on a diplomatic career. While occupying an influential position in French foreign trade diplomacy, Kojève worked on a series of manuscripts which largely remained unpublished until well after his death. Initially dismissed as post-historical irony and play, Kojève’s post-war philosophical writings open new perspectives on how we became post-historical and where we go from here.\n\nSpotlighting Kojeve's distinct contributions to legal scholarship, while also showcasing his broader influence across a range of disciplines — including philosophy, political theory, sociology, law and transnational studies — these two books include original contributions from eminent editors, translators, and biographers of Kojeve, as well as from historians of legal and political thought, specialists on global trade and private international law, statelessness, and public international law.\n\nFirst Panel - Kojève and the Ancients.\n\n* Participants: Jonas Schwab-Plfug, Luis Pedrazuela, and Teresa Pullano\n* Discussant: David Ragazzoni\n\nSecond Panel - Kojève and His Contemporaries.\n\n* Participants: Matthew Sharpe, Massimo Palma, and Igor Shoikhedbrod\n* Discussant: Clifford Orwin\n\nThird panel - Kojève and the Moderns. Between Kant and Hegel.\n\n* Participants: Bryan-Paul Frost and Jacob McNulty\n* Discussants: Alan Brudner and Susan Shell\n\nFourth panel - Kojève and Phenomenology.\n\n* Participants: William Conklin, Bogdan Ovcharuk, and Sabina Tortorella\n* Discussant: Tarek Dika.\n\nFifth panel - Kojève, Empire, and the Future of the Universal Homogeneous State.\n\n* Participants: Rob Howse and Olga Obolenets.\n* Discussants: Ronald Beiner and Melissa Williams\n\n**\\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\* \\***\n\nThis is a book launch on [Kojeve and Law: A Critical Examination](https://www.routledge.com/Kojeve-and-Law-A-Critical-Examination/Shoikhedbrod/p/book/9781032734118) (Routledge 2026) presented by the University of Toronto's Centre for Ethics. The conference is free to attend and open to the public. Talks will be streamed online with live chat.\n\nAbout the Centre for Ethics (http://ethics.utoronto.ca):\n\nThe Centre for Ethics is an interdisciplinary centre aimed at advancing research and teaching in the field of ethics, broadly defined. The Centre seeks to bring together the theoretical and practical knowledge of diverse scholars, students, public servants and social leaders in order to increase understanding of the ethical dimensions of individual, social, and political life.\n\nIn pursuit of its interdisciplinary mission, the Centre fosters lines of inquiry such as (1) foundations of ethics, which encompasses the history of ethics and core concepts in the philosophical study of ethics; (2) ethics in action, which relates theory to practice in key domains of social life, including bioethics, business ethics, and ethics in the public sphere; and (3) ethics in translation, which draws upon the rich multiculturalism of the City of Toronto and addresses the ethics of multicultural societies, ethical discourse across religious and cultural boundaries, and the ethics of international society.\n\nThe Ethics of A.I. Lab at the Centre For Ethics recently appeared on a list of 10 organizations leading the way in ethical A.I.: https://ocean.sagepub.com/blog/10-organizations-leading-the-way-in-ethical-ai","startDate":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Larkin Building, Room 200","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"15 Devonshire Place, University of Toronto, Toronto, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Ultimate Frisbee Pickup Game! (Weekly)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/30smidtownsingles/events/316629684/","description":"REBOOT - Exercise! Fun! Food! Drinks! This meetup has it all!\n\nThis ultimate frisbee meetup is a great way to make friends and get great exercise at the same time! What is ultimate frisbee? It's like soccer with a frisbee but with end zones like football. Come out and learn the ropes and have a good time. All skill levels welcome.\n\nAnd after frisbee is food and drinks! This meetup runs every week from May through September.\n\nThis event is co-hosted with the group 30SomethingsinToronto.\nhttps://www.meetup.com/30SomethingsinTO/events/\n\nA 1 time per season charge of $2 is collected for equipment costs (Cones & Pinneys).\n\nSchedule:\n6:30-7:15 Practice\n7:15-8:30 Games\n9:00 Food and Drinks at a nearby pub! (TBD)","startDate":"2026-10-09T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"David A. Balfour Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"75 Rosehill Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"30's Midtown Singles","url":"https://www.meetup.com/30smidtownsingles/"},"performer":"30's Midtown Singles"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"AWS YouthTech x SBG Sheridan Bootcamp","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-sheridan-college-davis-campus/events/316769723/","description":"**[Register now : AWS YouthTech X SBG Sheridan Bootcamp](https://luma.com/p3yhr7xo)**\n​Get ready for a high-energy afternoon at the AWS YouthTech × SBG Sheridan Bootcamp! Hosted by the AWS Student Builder Group at Sheridan College, this afternoon event is packed with learning, fresh ideas, and plenty of chances to explore what you can build with cloud and AI/ML technology. Whether you want to pick up practical skills, hear from people working with AWS, or spend a few hours in a room buzzing with momentum, there will be something worth showing up for.\n​Spots are limited-register early to secure yours!\n\n## ​**What to expect**\n\n* ​**Expert Sessions:** Hear directly from industry leaders and experienced AWS practitioners through cloud fundamentals talks, an AI/ML presentation, and an employee panel.\n* ​**Hands-on Workshop:** Roll up your sleeves and build real-world cloud and AI/ML skills in an interactive technical workshop.\n* ​**Kahoot & Prizes:** Join the fun and compete for a chance to win a coffee chat with a recruiter.\n* ​**Networking:** Connect with peers and professionals across the GTA who share your interest in cloud and tech.\n* ​**Resume drop at closing:** At the end of the event, attendees can submit their resume to a dedicated pool shared with recruiters.\n\n​*Come ready to learn, meet people, and make the most of an afternoon built for students who want a closer look at AWS and where it can take them.*\n\n## ​**Event Details**\n\n​**When:** Friday, October 9, 2026\n**Time:** 1:00 PM - 5:00 PM\n**Where: Room A145,** Sheridan HMC (Hazel McCallion Campus), Mississauga\n**Cost:** Free\n\nNOTE : [Luma](https://luma.com/p3yhr7xo) registration is required to confirm your spot. ONLY FOR ACTIVE STUDENTS FORM COLLEGES/UNIVERSITY ACROSS GTA","startDate":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Sheridan College - Hazel McCallion Campus","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4180 Duke of York Blvd, Mississauga, ON L5B 0H7, Canada, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AWS SBG at Sheridan College - Davis Campus","url":"https://www.meetup.com/aws-sbg-at-sheridan-college-davis-campus/"},"performer":"AWS SBG at Sheridan College - Davis Campus"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316628956/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-09T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free English Classes  - in-person at our Toronto school ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/events/316628967/","description":"Practise your English in a friendly, welcoming class in Toronto.\nJoin our free in-person English class and improve your speaking, fluency, grammar and vocabulary with supportive teachers. This class is a great opportunity to practise English, build confidence and meet new people.\n\n**When**\nEvery weekday Monday - Friday\n2.00pm–4.00pm\n\n**Where**\nTeaching House Toronto\nOHC / Sol Camps\n469 Jarvis St\nToronto, ON M4Y 2G8\nCanada\n\n[REGISTER NOW](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)\n\n**What you’ll practise**\n\n* Speaking and fluency\n* Grammar and vocabulary\n* Listening and pronunciation\n* Everyday English for real-life situations\n* Confidence using English with other people\n\n**Who can join?**\nAdults aged 18+ who want to improve their English. Refugees, asylum seekers and newcomers are very welcome.\n\n**About the classes**\nThe classes are taught by trainee English teachers on a Cambridge-accredited CELTA course and supervised by experienced teacher trainers.\n\n**Cost**\nFree\n\n**Before the class**\nPlease arrive a little early so we can welcome you and check your English level.\nSpaces may be limited, so please RSVP if you would like to attend.Cost: FREE\n\nSign up using this [registration form ](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)for automatic reminders and to be on our list for future classes.","startDate":"2026-10-09T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"http