s/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Waterworks Food Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"50 Brant St, Toronto, ON M5V 3G9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beethoven's Fifth with World Reknown Pianist Angela Hewitt + Pre-concert (TSO)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/events/316656578/","description":"On **Friday October 9th,** **join me to see** **internationally acclaimed Canadian Pianist and 2026/27 Spotlight Artist Angela Hewitt perform Beethoven’s Fourth Piano Concerto prior to the Orchestra's Fifth Symphony**. Jörg Widmann’s *Con brio* opens with a witty, high-spirited homage to Beethoven. Then, Hewitt brings poetic grace to Beethoven’s Fourth Piano Concerto, before the orchestra unleashes the composer’s thunderous Fifth Symphony—with the famous first four notes that changed classical music forever. Enhance your concert experience by arriving early for exquisite performances by the [TSO Chamber Soloists](https://www.tso.ca/about/orchestra/the-tso-chamber-soloists), thoughtfully curated by Jonathan Crow and included with the price of your ticket. My seat is Orchestra Right C34. **Purchase your own tickets for Beethoven's Fifth on Friday October 9th at 7:30pm. I can also extend my subscriber discount to members.**\n\n**PROGRAM**\n**Jörg Widmann**: *Con brio*\n\n**Beethoven**: Piano Concerto No. 4\n**Beethoven**: Symphony No. 5\n\n**COST**\nRegular: $70 - 208 includes taxes and fees.\n\nSubscriber additional tickets: $40 - 135 includes taxes and fees.\n\nRush: A limited number of tickets may go on sale at 1pm online, over the phone, or in-person at Roy Thomson Hall. Limit 2 per person based on availability.\n\nMeetup fee: $5\n\nTicket Policy: Sales are final and non-refundable.\n\n***\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **Simply RSVP Yes, [purchase](https://my.tso.ca/3966/3992) your ticket and post your seat number and I will move you to attending.**\n* If you'd like a discounted ticket, please message me after you RSVP with your preferred seating location. I will confirm the subscriber discount price, and once you send an etransfer, your ticket will be purchased and provided in person at event start time.\n* If you plan to buy RUSH, please state that in your RSVP, so I can include you in the pre-mail and we can meet you.\n* RSVPs close 2 days prior, and cancellations after will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n* A reminder will go out the day before with my cell and details when to meet, etc.\n\n‐‐----‐----‐‐-------------‐-----------\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for the Pre-Concert at: 5:45pm** **at Roy Thomson Hall at 60 Simcoe St., inside the southern-most double set of glass doors, after scanning your tickets. There are a limited number of seats in the choir loft, so get there on time to get a seat and sit together.**\n\n**Pre-concert start time: 6:15pm**\n\n**Meet me for the Concert at: 7:15pm** **at Roy Thomson Hall at 60 Simcoe St., inside the southern-most double set of glass doors, after scanning your tickets.**\n\n**Concert start time: 7:30pm**\n\nEnjoy and please post your Comments after!","startDate":"2026-10-09T21:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Roy Thomson Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"60 Simcoe St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Experience Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/experiencetoronto/"},"performer":"Experience Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎬Movie: Other Mommy  -  Food & Drinks after the movie 🍿!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316155472/","description":"🎬 Let’s Go to the Movies (and Actually Talk… or Not)\n\nWhether you're a film nerd, popcorn enthusiast, or just looking for a chill night out with interesting people — this one's for you.\n\nWe’re heading out to see a movie together, then grabbing food or drinks after. If the film's great (or terrible), we’ll probably talk about it forever. If it’s just okay, we’ll talk about it for 10 minutes and move on to everything else — books, dating apps, weird dreams, how Toronto keeps getting more expensive, etc.\n\nThe vibe is relaxed, friendly, and not too serious. No film degree needed. No icebreakers. No pressure to “perform.” Just come enjoy the film, connect with some thoughtful people, and see where the night goes Click here to watch trailer!\n\n🎞️ **Movie Title + Trailer:**[ \\[Click here to watch trailer!\\]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pPxrX9ukWBY)\n\n📖 **📖 Plot Summary:** A terrifying, supernatural trip into the darkening world of a young girl as her family, and their home, are haunted by a sinister entity that is determined to take up residence inside her. But first, it needs to persuade her to let it in …\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ **Event Details**\n\n📍 **Meetup Time:** 6:00 PM (Final time + theatre announced Tuesday of event week)\n🎬 **Movie Start Time:** TBA\n⏱️ **Runtime:** TBA\n📌 **Meetup Spot:** To be confirmed (based on theatre)\n🎟️ **Cost:**\n\n* **$11.50** for *CineClub* members\n* **$16.00** regular admission\n👉 You are responsible for buying your own ticket.\n\n**🪑 Reserved Seating:**\nYou must buy your ticket *before* signing up. You'll be asked where you're sitting so we can all sit together! However, members are welcome to sit anywhere that works for them.\n🎫 Buy your ticket here: [https://www.cineplex.com](https://www.cineplex.com)\n📍🪑 **Where I will be sitting:**\n\n🍿 **After the Movie:**\nYes, we’re heading out after! It’s not just a movie night — it’s a social night. Let's talk, laugh, and dissect every plot twist.\n\n***\n\n### ✅ **Before You Sign Up**\n\n* Please **buy your ticket first** — seating is limited!\n* When signing up, let us know your **seat number** so we can try to group everyone together.\n* You can still sign up or just **show up on the day** if you’re not sure you can make it — we’re flexible!\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)\n🎟️ **Join Cineplex’s CineClub for discounts**: [https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub](https://www.cineplex.com/cineclub)\n🎁 **Get your SCENE Card** for free movies and points: [https://www.scene.ca](https://www.scene.ca)\n\n***\n\n### 🎥 **A Quick Word About Movie Etiquette**\n\nWe love a great film experience. Please:\n\n* Turn off your phone\n* Don’t talk during the movie\n* Be respectful of others\n\nRepeat offenders will be removed from the group — we take our cinema seriously (but with snacks).\n\n***\n\n### 👥 **About the Group**\n\nThis event is open to everyone — single, not single, shy, social, new in town or a long-time local. We're a group for people who love movies *and* making real connections. We also do walks, hikes, restaurants, arts & culture — come be part of it!\n🎬 **Organized by:** Mathew\n📧 Questions? Reach out: **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Cuddle Club - platonic body nourishing.","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316629411/","description":"**CUDDLE CLUB.**\n**Have you tried that?**\n\n**In Amsterdam cuddle events are sold out quickly. Even few different Cuddle clubs are happening at the same day. It's so popular there.**\n\n**In Toronto there** **is** **nearly no Cuddle clubs yet.**\n**But we are doing that.**\n**Join our tantric group and leave a message in comments if you wanna join the waiting list.**\n**T.me/TorontoTantra**\n**___**\n**About this event**\n**• What is the cuddle club?**\n\n**It’s a cozy evening to experience how deeply nourishing it can feel to be held, without any romantic or sexual expectations. A space where people can come together to share love and touch. We cuddle platonically, the way you’d hold a child or a kitten.**\n\n**• What will we be doing?**\n\n**Facilitator will guide you through some gentle exercises to help you unwind after your day, soften into your body, and calm your nervous system. We aim to make you feel safe in your own body, which can help you connect with others.**\n\n**• Cuddle puddle perfection**\n\n**Everything is by invitation, but we will guide you into a beautifully structured cuddle puddle. It is a very comfortable, welcoming way of cuddling where you are held and touched by multiple people at the same time. Chances are you’ll float home afterwards, high on oxytocin.**\n\n**• Important terms & agreements:**\n1. **Keep it platonic: we cuddle without romantic or sexual expectations or escalations**\n1. **Take care of yourself and others: communicate and respect boundaries**\n1. **Be here fully: This is a sober space. No drugs, no alcohol. No phones.**\n\n**Details in telegram group:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n**Regular Ticket — $50 CAD**\n**Early Bird Ticket — $35 CAD (If you register and pay before August 31).**\n**Supportive Ticket — $25 CAD (For students and people with low financial income).**\n**Combo — $60 CAD for 2 people (Bring a friend).**\n\n**Free participation.**\n**We want everyone to have an opportunity to participate. If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Mississauga- let’s speak French/ Parlons français","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/events/314154988/","description":"Let’s get together to speak French! We’ll enjoy tea/coffee and some icebreaker games. Everyone is welcome.\n\nVenez parler français!\n\nÀ bientôt,\n\nHassane.\n\n\\*Merci beaucoup de vous être inscrit(e) à notre prochaine rencontre! Nous sommes ravis de votre présence.\nAfin de permettre à d’autres de se joindre à nous, nous vous demandons respectueusement :\n\n1. **Si vos plans changent,** veuillez mettre à jour votre statut (passer à 'Non') le plus rapidement possible pour libérer votre place.\n2. **Si vous êtes sur la liste d'attente,** merci de ne pas vous présenter à l'événement. Votre statut doit être confirmé pour pouvoir participer. Veuillez vous inscrire directement aux prochaines dates disponibles.\n\nAu plaisir de vous accueillir!\n\n\\*To allow others to join us, we respectfully ask that you:\n\n* **If your plans change,** please update your RSVP status (change it to 'No') as quickly as possible to free up your spot.\n* **If you are on the waiting list,** please do not show up for the event. Your status must be confirmed to participate. Instead, please register directly for the next available dates.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nVeuillez noter que pour profiter pleinement de nos échanges, une aptitude de base à la conversation est vivement souhaitée : ce groupe est un cercle de discussion convivial et non un cours de langue.\n\nPlease note that to fully enjoy the experience, a basic speaking aptitude is recommended: this group is a social conversation circle, not a formal teaching class.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming you!\n\nPlease join our WhatsApp group:\n\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/LRUdXbjpG8I9aph4dU6Go8","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chocolate and love cafe","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"5985 Rodeo Dr Unit 14, Mississauga, ON L5R 3V6,, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/diskuto/"},"performer":"Diskuto - Talk with Language Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/events/316629514/","description":"### **Friday Dink & Strategy Clinic (1hr Lesson + Optional 1hr Game)**\n\n* **6:00 PM - 7:00 PM:** Pickleball Dink & Strategy Clinic (GTA Pickleball Lessons)\n* **7:00 PM - 8:00 PM (Optional):** Extra hour of game play available for an extra $5 per person. (Note: The optional extra hour (7-8 PM) requires at least 4 players to agree and depends on court availability. Please let me know early if you are interested!)\n\n**Are you ready to elevate your pickleball game?** Join our exclusive, small-group clinic designed for players who want to move beyond just hitting hard and master the soft game. If you want to improve your dinking, court positioning, and stacking strategies, this session is perfect for you!\n\n**Meet Your Instructor** Hi, I'm Jeong, an NCCP-certified Level 2 pickleball and tennis instructor based in the GTA. I focus on helping players build solid technical fundamentals and strategic court awareness to win more rallies.\n\n**Verified Coach Profiles & Reviews**\n\n* [Superprof.ca](https://www.superprof.ca/nccp-certified-tennis-pickleball-instructor-teaching-the-basic-theory-and-practical-skills-tennis-pickl.html)\n* [Teachme.to](https://teachme.to/listings/pickleball/pickleball-with-jeong-sohn?skill=pickleball&latitude=43.866955&longitude=-79.440567)\n* [Playtogether.ca](https://playtogether.ca/about/)\n\n**What to Expect (60-Minute Session):**\n\n* **Warm-up & Assessment:** Quick rallies to assess your current level and identify key areas for improvement.\n* **Core Skills Training:** Step-by-step drills focusing on dink consistency, tactical positioning, and an introduction to stacking strategies.\n* **Guided Match Play:** Apply what you've learned in organized mini-games with real-time, personalized feedback.\n\n**Event Details:**\n\n* **Location:** Swing Star (5 Connie Crescent Unit 1, Vaughan, ON)\n* **Date & Time:** Every (Fri) 6-7pm\n* **Skill Level:** Beginner to Low-Intermediate\n* **Spots Available:** Strictly limited to 6-8 players to ensure quality coaching.\n* **Fee:** $20 (Covers court usage, practice balls, and instruction).\n* **Min-Max** Students: 3-6 (If there are fewer than 3 registrations, the amount paid via PayPal will be refunded via e-Transfer)\n* **Optional Extra Hour**: If you'd like to stay and play games after the 6-7 PM lesson, an additional hour (7-8 PM) is available for just **$5 per person**. This option is available if at least 4 players stay!","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Swing Star - Indoor Golf And Pickleball","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Vaughan","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1-15 Connie Crescent,, Vaughan, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels","url":"https://www.meetup.com/playtogether/"},"performer":"Play Together Pickleball GTA for all levels"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Casual Board Games and Pub Social After","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/events/316441924/","description":"The Board Games event is a fun, sociable and charitable event\n\nWe are a fun, friendly and kind group of people mostly in our 20s, 30s and 40s. Beginners are welcome! We are a very inclusive and social group and we teach people how to play games they have not played before :)\n\nWe provide a variety of 40+ board games. The games usually take 5 or 10 minutes to learn and 30 to 60 minutes to play.\n\nPlay in French: On the last Friday of the month, we're offering a table where the games are played in French. Anyone with an intermediate level of French who wants to practice while playing is welcome to join. Just ask for Philippe when you arrive.\n\n**Time**\n\n*Board Games Start time: 630pm\n- Board Games end time: 10pm\n*Eat / Drink/ Socialise at a nearby pub afterwards\n\n**Location**\n\n30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8 (Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection)\n\nThe entrance to the board game room is at the back of the Church. There is a sign on the door that says BOARD GAMES GROUP.\n\nPlease use the map provided on the event page also.\n\nPayment\n**There are two ways to pay**\n**10 by Cash - coins are not accepted. Only bills.****\n**11.55 by Debit/Credit card\n\n**Charity Donations**\n\n- This is a not-for-profit initiative. Revenue go towards covering costs of the event including venue, insurance marketing, refreshments and board games. Any surplus revenue is donated to charity\n\n**Food and drink**\n\n*Everyone will get cookies/candy for free\n- Cups will be provided for tap water\n*Bring your own food and drink.\n- Please do not bring CHIPS AND CRACKERS as they make a mess and are greasy\n***ALCOHOL IS PROHIBITED AND WE HAVE A ZERO TOLERANCE POLICY ON THIS - there are no second chances**\n\nPhotos will be taken at the event and posted publicly for marketing purposes. Please only attend if you are ok with this or tell me when you arrive that you do not want to be in any photos\n\nThe event is officially hosted by Ace of Math Learning Program Ontario Inc.","startDate":"2026-10-09T22:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Ukrainian Catholic Church of the Holy Protection","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"30 Leeds St, Toronto, ON M6G 3R8, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Board Games and Social","url":"https://www.meetup.com/boardgamestoronto/"},"performer":"Board Games and Social"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/2/8/6/highres_535829318.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/e/4/7/highres_471324135.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/ph